Article 12
Prevention of violence against women as referred to in Article 11 letter a is carried out through:
a. implementation of policies, programs and activities for the prevention of violence against women involving parties within the regional scope;
b. provision of education on the prevention of violence against women in the region;
c. enhancement of community participation, business sector, and media in the prevention of violence against women in the region; and
d. creation and/or utilization of the Citizen Information System application in submitting reports of cases of violence against women and children.

Article 14
The provision of services for women victims of violence as referred to in Article 11 letter b shall be carried out through:
a. implementation of service provision for women victims of violence through UPTD P3AP2KB or work units handling PPA affairs that require coordination in the region;
b. provision of public complaint services for women victims of violence in the region;
c. provision of outreach services for women victims of violence in the region;
d. provision of case management services for women victims of violence at the district/regency regional level;
e. provision of temporary shelter services for women victims of violence in the region;
f. provision of mediation services for women victims of violence in the region;
g. provision of assistance services for women victims of violence in the region;
h. provision of service facilities and infrastructure for women victims of violence in the region;
i. provision of information infrastructure available in public spaces; and
j. developing an emergency system responsive to the occurrence of acts of violence against women and children through applications.

Article 26
Prevention of violence against Children as referred to in Article 25 letter a is carried out through:
a. implementation of policies, programs and activities for prevention of violence against Children requiring special protection involving government and non-government institutions in the region;
b. provision of education on prevention of violence against Children requiring special protection in the region;
c. enhancement of community participation through the Community-Based Integrated Child Protection (PATBM) movement, business sector, media and children in violence prevention in the region; and
d. strengthening cooperation to realize Child-Friendly Regency (KLA), Child-Friendly Sub-district (Kelana), and Child-Friendly Village (Dela).

CHAPTER VIII
COMMUNITY PARTICIPATION
Article 44
(1) The community, Family and/or parents may participate in the implementation of women's empowerment and child protection.
(2) The community as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be carried out individually or institutionally.
(3) Community participation as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be carried out, among others, by:
a. establishing women's empowerment and child protection units within community organizations, community-based child protection, or professional organizations;
b. conducting socialization regarding women's empowerment, prevention of violence against women and children as well as child protection;
c. conducting prevention of acts of violence within the community environment; and
d. providing information and/or reporting the occurrence of violence, discrimination, exploitation, and human rights violations against women and Children to the competent authorities if violence against women and Children occurs in their environment;
e. optimizing the function of community organizations such as PKK, integrated service institutions for the protection of women and children in the Region;
f. conducting socialization and education on laws and regulations related to women's empowerment, protection of women and Children, such as prevention of unregistered marriages and the dangers of child marriage;
g. providing input in the process of formulating regional laws and regulations;
h. prohibiting the occurrence of unregistered marriages;
i. providing space for Children to gather and organize to express themselves and convey their opinions; and
j. supervising Children in accessing various information.

Article 5
(1) The technical implementation of services by the Regional Apparatus administering governmental affairs in the field of Women's Empowerment and Child Protection, in providing services for women and children who experience problems of violence, discrimination, special protection, and other problems, shall be carried out by UPTD P3AP2KB.
(2) UPTD P3AP2KB as referred to in paragraph (1) shall carry out service functions:
a. public complaints;
b. victim outreach;
c. case management;
d. temporary shelter;
e. mediation; and
f. victim assistance.
(3) In the implementation of service functions as referred to in paragraph (2) letter b, a task force for women's empowerment and child protection may be formed, facilitated by the Regional Apparatus responsible for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection.
(4) Service functions provided by UPTD P3AP2KB as referred to in paragraph (2) shall refer to service standards that have been established in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

Article 3
The implementation of women's empowerment and child protection aims to:
a. realize opportunities in access, participation, control, and benefits in development and control of resources in the Region;
b. prevent and handle violence, exploitation, and discriminatory treatment against women and children;
c. improve the quality and role of women and children; and
d. provide available data for planning women's empowerment as well as fulfillment and protection of children's rights.

REGENT OF BIMA
WEST NUSA TENGGARA PROVINCE
REGIONAL REGULATION OF BIMA REGENCY
NUMBER 5 OF 2019
CONCERNING
THE IMPLEMENTATION OF WOMEN'S EMPOWERMENT AND
CHILD PROTECTION
BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD
THE REGENT OF BIMA,
Considering : a. that every person including women and children has the right to the fulfillment of rights and protection from violence, exploitation, and discriminatory treatment in order to provide security and comfort;
b. that in order to fulfill the rights and protection of women and children from violence, exploitation, and discriminatory treatment in Bima Regency, the role of the regional government is required in its implementation;
c. that the implementation of protection for women and children needs to be given direction and foundation to ensure legal certainty based on the principle of justice;
d. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b, and letter c, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning the Implementation of Women's Empowerment and Child Protection;
In View of : 1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;
2. Law Number 69 of 1958 concerning the Establishment of Level II Regions within the Level I Regional Areas of Bali, West Nusa Tenggara and East Nusa Tenggara (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1958 Number 122, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 1655);
3. Law Number 7 of 1984 concerning Ratification of the Convention on the Elimination of All Forms of Discrimination Against Women (Convention on the Elimination of All Forms Of Discrimination Against Women) (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1984 Number 29, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3277);
4. Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2002 Number 109, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4235) as has been amended several times, most recently by Law Number 17 of 2016 concerning Stipulation of Government Regulation in Lieu of Law Number 1 of 2016 concerning the Second Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection into Law (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2016 Number 99, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5882);
5. Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 244, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5587) as has been amended several times, most recently by Law Number 9 of 2015 concerning the Second Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2015 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5679);
6. Government Regulation Number 12 of 2017 concerning Guidance and Supervision of Regional Government Administration (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2017 Number 73, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 6041);
7. Regulation of the Minister of Home Affairs Number 15 of 2008 concerning General Guidelines for the Implementation of Gender Mainstreaming in the Regions as has been amended by Regulation of the Minister of Home Affairs Number 67 of 2011 concerning Amendment to Regulation of the Minister of Home Affairs Number 15 of 2008 concerning General Guidelines for the Implementation of Gender Mainstreaming in the Regions (State News of the Republic of Indonesia of 2011 Number 927);
8. Regulation of the Minister of Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 4 of 2018 concerning Guidelines for the Establishment of Regional Technical Implementation Units for the Protection of Women and Children (State News of the Republic of Indonesia of 2018 Number 532);
9. Regional Regulation of West Nusa Tenggara Province Number 8 of 2015 concerning the Implementation of Protection for Women and Children (Regional Gazette of West Nusa Tenggara Province of 2015 Number 8, Supplement to the Regional Gazette of West Nusa Tenggara Province Number 119);
With Mutual Agreement

